# EGT sweep artefacts: the BULK is reproducible output, but a thin slice is
# tracked on purpose so a collaborator can re-cut the analysis without a ~3h
# regeneration (and without a working Lean build).
#
# One `(t, α)` sweep writes hundreds of files per run — parquet face tables,
# GEXF/PNG/SVG invasion graphs, replicator basins, per-stage reports. Those
# regenerate exactly (the run directory name embeds a hash of the cells
# analysed), so they stay out.
#
# What IS tracked, and why (these are exactly the inputs the four analysis
# modules in `pd_runner.egt` read — see the module docstrings):
#   runs/*/summary.json                     `integrity` + `analysis` (tidy.csv,
#                                           phase_maps, family_diffs) read ONLY
#                                           this; it is complete and
#                                           self-describing
#   runs/*/*/assumptions.json               `integrity.scan_assumptions` globs
#                                           one level (`*/assumptions.json`) for
#                                           truncation + cross-check markers
#   runs/*/moran/stationary.json            `findings` drills into this for the
#                                           full (M, β) table
#   runs/*/ess/payoff_matrix_numeric.csv    `nash_structure` (diagonal > 0 ⇔
#                                           self-play (C,C))
#   runs/*/nash/**/equilibria.jsonl         `nash_structure` classifies NE
#                                           components by cooperation_rate_float
#   runs/*/nash/latest                      symlink into nash/runs/<ts>/; the
#                                           `_latest_nash` fast path (it falls
#                                           back to globbing nash/runs/* anyway)
#   analysis/                               the derived artefacts + figures — the
#                                           first thing a reader opens
#   sweep_summary*.json                     grid → matrix dedup record
#
# Deliberately NOT tracked though it looks similar: `replicator/basins.json`
# (~920K) — no module in the analysis layer reads it; basin numbers reach the
# analysis via `summary.json`'s `stages.replicator`.
#
# `runs/**` (not `runs/`) is load-bearing: a directory-level exclude stops git
# descending, and every `!` negation below it would silently do nothing. The
# `!runs/*/` + `!runs/*/*/` directory re-includes are what let the leaf
# negations match at all.
#
# Keep a fuller result set by copying it out, or point `--out-root` elsewhere.
runs/**
!runs/*/
!runs/*/summary.json
!runs/*/*/
!runs/*/*/assumptions.json
!runs/*/moran/stationary.json
!runs/*/ess/payoff_matrix_numeric.csv
!runs/*/nash/latest
!runs/*/nash/runs/
!runs/*/nash/runs/*/
!runs/*/nash/runs/*/equilibria.jsonl

report.html

# Frozen pre-paper artefact archives (2026-09-01): kept out of git, backed by
# OneDrive. The tarball is the machine-readable record behind TAUBOTS.md §4's
# pre-freeze EGT observations (retired zoos, pre-rename bot names).
archive/
